[h1]Better Commerce Screen UI by Najane[/h1]

Reworks the Commerce screen - Resources, Trade Routes, Empire, and a new Factory tab - into something you can actually read and act on in one pass. [b]No rules change[/b]: everything here you could already do by hand, just far slower.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]What you get[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Right-click to unassign[/b], hold [b]Shift[/b] for every resource of that kind, and Shift-assign to fill a settlement in one click.
[*][b]Assign All / Reassign All / Unassign All[/b], plus a priority picker and quick-assign per settlement.
[*][b]Optional automation[/b] on resources arriving with the screen closed - off by default.
[*][b]Camels handled correctly[/b] - the extra slots they grant are never lost mid-reshuffle.
[*][b]Trade route cards[/b] rebuilt: origin, destination and domain on one line, three cards to a row, a running total of routes you hold vs. could still open.
[*][b]Filter tabs per section[/b] - show only routes carrying Food, Production, Gold, Science, Culture, Influence, Camels, or Empire/Treasure resources, richest first.
[*][b]Buy and send a Merchant straight from a route card[/b] - one click, walks there on its own, opens the route itself. Warns you when a leader's trade capacity is already spoken for, and links straight to diplomacy with them.
[*][b]Empire resources shown in numbers[/b] - not "+1 Gold in all settlements" but what that is actually worth to your empire.
[*][b]A new Factory Resources tab[/b] (Modern age): what's slotted, what's idle, what each is worth.
[*][b]A running GDP total[/b] toward the Economic Victory, broken down by source.
[*][b]Treasure convoys[/b] without every homeland settlement cluttering the "not generating" list.
[*][b]A calmer screen[/b] overall - icon tabs, no instruction paragraphs, no nags for resources that have nowhere to go.
[/list]

Assignment logic weighs Happiness rescues, each settlement's chosen priority, and every conditional bonus in the game's own data - a resource that only pays with a Port, your capital, or a certain building is never credited where it would not fire.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

Saved games are unaffected and [b]no rules, values or balance change[/b] - safe to add or remove mid-game.

⚠️ [b]Not compatible with Resource+[/b]. Both replace the same screen; run one or the other.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Credits[/h2]

The automatic-assignment engine is a port of [b]Resource+[/b] by [b]Br4d[/b], used with permission - this mod exists because that one showed what was possible.

[b]Open source[/b], written in full by [b]Opus 5[/b] (Anthropic), free for anyone to reuse:
